I also gave the trade a little bit of room

475
00:22:40,850 --> 00:22:43,902
to the downside, which is why when I opened it, the SPX was around 620.

476
00:22:44,120 --> 00:22:49,415
So I had about a 10 point wiggle room to the downside for my break even at expiration.

477
00:22:49,415 --> 00:22:52,380
And this is the way or at least the style in which I really like to trade.

478
00:22:52,380 --> 00:22:54,490
I like to give my positions a little bit

479
00:22:54,490 --> 00:22:57,304
of wiggle room to the downside, which is why I prefer butterflies.

480
00:22:57,305 --> 00:23:01,680
I like the fact that it has the asymmetrical returns if it ends up being a pin.

481
00:23:01,680 --> 00:23:05,250
Another trader might sell puts below this level. That would be a great approach.

482
00:23:05,250 --> 00:23:11,115
Also, selling an at-the-money put or something that's slightly out-the-money is a decent approach, but it's also aggressive.

483
00:23:11,115 --> 00:23:15,545
Selling an out-the-money put in a situation like this is a really high probability of success.

484
00:23:15,545 --> 00:23:16,755
Or you can just buy a call.

485
00:23:16,755 --> 00:23:20,046
But the problem with when you buy a call is if the market is

486
00:23:20,046 --> 00:23:23,337
pretty flat for a good bit of time, even if you're a right and

487
00:23:23,337 --> 00:23:29,684
the market does bounce, you sometimes go a little crazy, or at least I do, just waiting for the move to happen if it takes too long.

488
00:23:29,685 --> 00:23:33,330
So in days like this where I don't have massive conviction in a rapid

489
00:23:33,330 --> 00:23:35,933
or a very aggressive momentum-based bounce, I'd much rather go

490
00:23:35,933 --> 00:23:39,578
with something like a butterfly and not have to worry so much about the

491
00:23:39,580 --> 00:23:43,880
0DTE time decay. Or even better, use that time decay in my favor.

492
00:23:43,880 --> 00:23:46,691
And this would be in my favor if the market

493
00:23:46,691 --> 00:23:49,502
was just to be choppy and time was to pass

494
00:23:49,502 --> 00:23:51,470
by as it remained around this strike

495
00:23:51,470 --> 00:23:55,406
of 620, which was about the equivalent of the power strike of 600 on the SPX.

